#BlueJ class context
comment0.target=Animal
comment0.text=\n\ An\ Animal\ object\ is\ an\ animal\ character,\ displayed\ on\ the\ screen\n\ that\ can\ \n\ \ \ go\ left,\n\ \ \ go\ right,\n\ \ \ jump,\n\ \ \ speak,\ "think"\ or\ shout\ a\ phrase,\n\ \ \ introduce\ itself.\n
comment1.params=typeOfAnimal\ nameOfAnimal\ x\ y
comment1.target=Animal(java.lang.String,\ java.lang.String,\ double,\ double)
comment1.text=\n\ Constructor\ requires\n\ \ -\ the\ type\ of\ animal,\n\ \ -\ the\ name\ of\ the\ animal,\n\ \ -\ and\ the\ coordinates\ (left,\ top)\ of\ where\ it\ should\ be\ placed.\n\ \ \ \ For\ example\n\ \ \ \ new\ Animal("dog",\ "Scruff",\ 100,\ 50);\n
